# A single zero is pushed onto the stack (preference)

Standing user preference: A single zero is pushed onto the stack before the first line of the file is read; this sentinel value is never popped.

## Conventions
- A single zero is pushed onto the stack before the first line of the file is read; this sentinel value is never popped.

